  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A car accelerates uniformly. The car passes point X at time t<sub>1</sub> with velocity v<sub>1</sub> and point Y at time t<sub>2</sub> with velocity v<sub>2</sub>. The distance XY is s.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The following expressions are proposed for the magnitude of its acceleration a:</p>\n<p>I.    <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a=\\frac{2s}{t_{2}-t_{1}^{2}}\"></span></p>\n<p>II.   <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a=\\frac{v_{2}^{2}-v_{1}^{2}}{2s}\"></span></p>\n<p>III.  <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a=\\frac{v_{2}-v_{1}}{t_{2}-t_{1}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Which is correct?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">I and II only</li><li data-label=\"B\">I and III only</li><li data-label=\"C\">II and III only</li><li data-label=\"D\">I, II and III</li></ol>"
  },
